+    done-callback: the run goes on writing checkpoints until it reaches its
+    next step, so deleting them any earlier would leave the rest behind.
+
+    A run that never started wrote nothing, and its callback runs on the
+    event loop, which a database call would block.
+    """
+    if not run.cancelled():
+        _discard_checkpoints(agent, event_id)
